gadb(){return"Guide"},
gadk(){return"Basics"},
gadj(){return"Advanced & hidden features"},
gadq(){return"Tap an available table to start a new order, or an occupied one to reopen it.\nTap the list icon to switch between the floor plan and a simple list view.\nTable colour shows status at a glance \u2014 green free, orange occupied, red needs attention.\nTap the calendar icon to open Bookings without leaving the floor plan."},
gadp(){return'In Edit layout mode, long-press a table to move, rotate, resize, duplicate, or delete it.\nLong-press a chair on an active table to name it \u2014 useful for splitting the bill by name later.\nTap the link icon to combine tables into one order for a large party; drag to arrange, then tap Done.\nIn list view, drag the handle to reorder tables; the link-off icon un-combines a group.\nWhile editing, tap the small "?" next to Done editing to replay the full edit-mode walkthrough.'},
gadg(){return"Courses like Starters and Mains sit at the top level \u2014 tap one to see its items or subcategories.\nUse the drag handle to reorder categories and items.\nTap + to add a new course, subcategory, or item."},
gadf(){return"Subcategories can be limited to specific days or service periods, e.g. a lunch-only category.\nA subcategory can be assigned to one specific menu, so it only appears there \u2014 not on every menu.\nAllergen badges are tooltip-only today \u2014 tap and hold one to see the full allergen name.\nSet-menu pricing tiers are configured under Menus, and get auto-detected at billing time."},
gadi(){return"Browse categories along the bar and tap an item to add it to the order.\nTap Send to fire new items to the kitchen or bar \u2014 sent items lock and can't be edited directly.\nFor takeaway, choose cash or card before sending the order."},
gadh(){return"Marking an item's course \u2014 starter, main, dessert \u2014 drives set-menu tier pricing automatically at billing time.\nTap an added item to adjust modifiers or apply an override, if it supports one.\nUse Void with a reason instead of deleting an item once it's already been sent.\nAssign items to a chair as you add them, so the bill can be split by person later."},
gada(){return"Tap + to create a new booking for a date and time.\nUse the date strip or the calendar icon to jump to a different day.\nTap a booking to seat the customer once they arrive."},
gad9(){return"A walk-in with no reservation can be logged the same way, so it still counts toward customer history.\nA booking left unseated past its time is automatically flagged as a no-show.\nTap the people icon to see a customer's full booking history and notes.\nThe Timeline tab shows the whole day's bookings against your tables at a glance."},
gad7(){return"Review the order total, then choose a payment method to settle the bill.\nTap the + icon to jump back to the order screen and add more items before paying."},
gad6(){return"Tap the split icon to divide the bill \u2014 by named seat if chairs were named, equally by headcount, or item-by-item otherwise.\nIf the table ordered a set menu, tap the menu-book icon to auto-detect and apply the right pricing tier.\nUse the replay icon to quickly add another round of the same drinks.\nThe history icon shows a full audit trail of any voids, comps, or reopened bills for this order."},
gado(){return"Browse stock items and their current counts \u2014 low-stock items are flagged.\nTap + to add a new stock item."},
gadn(){return"Use the scan icon to book in a delivery by barcode, or the checklist icon for items without one.\nLink a stock item to a menu item's recipe so sales automatically deduct stock.\nSome modifiers can override which stock item they deduct from, independent of the base recipe.\nManage suppliers from their own icon here, and track incoming deliveries in batches.\nOwners and admins can tap the shopping-list icon to see what needs reordering."},
gadm(){return"Venue profile, opening hours, and your team list are the everyday settings here.\nUse the search box at the top to jump straight to a setting by name."},
gadl(){return"Sync & Devices controls the relay connection and which device is primary or backup master \u2014 most venues never need to touch this.\nInvite Device, under Team, generates a QR code to add a new device to the venue without typing anything.\nKitchen printers and stations are configured under Service, not directly here.\nDanger Zone, in red, holds irreversible actions like resetting venue data \u2014 treat with care.\nDemo mode lets you load or clear sample data for training, without touching real orders."},
gXU(){return'Tickets appear as orders are sent from the floor \u2014 tap Bump when an item or order is ready.\nUse the station filter to show only tickets for your station, or "All stations" for everything.'},
gadc(){return"The bell icon sends an urgent call to the floor \u2014 use it only when something needs attention now.\nThe overflow menu holds recently bumped tickets, today's pre-orders, and the full service history.\nSwitching stations changes which tickets you can see, not which orders actually exist."},
gade(){return"This is the same Kitchen Display screen, filtered to show only drink-course items."},
gad8(){return"Named split uses the chair labels below; no names yet? Use the equal-split stepper, or switch to an itemised split."},
